    "description": "The Z6 e-Steer is EGO's 42-inch zero turn with a steering wheel in place of the usual lap bars, which removes the biggest learning curve in the category. EGO's spec sheet lists a 12-gauge stamped steel deck, 10 cutting heights from 1.5 to 4.5 inches, blade speed adjustable from 2,300 to 3,200 RPM, up to 8 mph in Sport mode, and up to 2 acres per charge on the included six-battery kit: two 56V 10.0Ah and four 6.0Ah packs with an 800W charger. Cruise control is unique to the e-Steer models. The warranty is 5 years or 300 hours on the mower and up to 5 years on the batteries with registration. It is the most expensive way to buy a 42-inch zero turn, and the case for it is quiet, no engine maintenance and the steering. See our electric zero turn guide for EGO's lap-bar models and the rest of the battery class."
