          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a 42 inch zero turn better than a 42 inch lawn tractor?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "On a flat or gently rolling lawn with trees and beds, yes: a zero turn is faster and leaves much less trimming. A lawn tractor is better on slopes, for towing and for owners who never want to learn lap bars. Our zero turn vs riding mower comparison covers the trade-off in detail."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are electric 42 inch zero turns as good as gas?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For cut quality and speed on a lawn within their rated acreage, they are competitive. EGO rates the Z6 e-Steer for up to 2 acres per charge. They cost considerably more, and when the battery runs out the mowing stops until it recharges, so they suit lawns comfortably inside the rated range."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do 42 inch zero turns come with a fabricated deck?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A few do. Of the machines on this list, the Cub Cadet Ultima Z2 42 has a fabricated 11-gauge deck and the Husqvarna Z242F Special Edition a fabricated 10-gauge deck. Most other 42-inch models, including the Toro TimeCutter and Troy-Bilt Mustang Z42, use stamped decks."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "The Honest Reviewers" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
